<Base title="About" activePage="about">
  <h1 class="page-title">About</h1>
  <div class="body-text">
    <p>
      I'm a second-year PhD student at ETH Zurich working on video generation
      and world models, with a focus on autonomous driving. My research asks
      how temporal consistency emerges — or fails to emerge — in learned
      generative models, and what this tells us about how machines understand
      the physical world.
    </p>
    <p>
      My primary platform is Orbis, a spatiotemporal diffusion transformer
      I built for generating driving videos. Through it, I explore questions
      about representation learning, feature alignment, and the geometry of
      video data — ideas that connect to the manifold hypothesis and active
      inference in ways I find intellectually compelling.
    </p>
    <p>
      Outside research, I make ambient and textural electronic music using
      Eurorack modular synthesis, gravitating toward granular processing
      of the human voice. I believe in minimalism as methodology: in
      research, in music, in how I structure my tools and my time.
    </p>
    <a href="/cv.pdf" class="cv-link">↓ Download CV (PDF)</a>
  </div>
</Base>
